  "behavior": [
    "The already-committed host replies to valid late lobby READY while Doom configures, using the original session/seed token and roster.",
    "Shared group parsing checks framing, sender, token, count and reserved bytes; session and route validation happen before the helper.",
    "Replies are limited to ten per second per peer and stop after configuration.",
    "Lobby READY does not satisfy engine readiness. Every engine must send GCAREADY before the host produces canonical ticks.",
    "A peer that remains in the lobby triggers the existing 30-second configuration failure without delivering ticks.",
    "Existing wire format, game protocol 4 and eight-second guest lobby timeout are preserved. Native-game handoff is unchanged."
  ],
